      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The experience of a solo practitioner suggests that the incidence of multiple myeloma is higher than the widely reported figure of 2.7/100,000. Only by early recognition and treatment will the survival rate be increased. Measurement of the sedimentation rate may be helpful in spotting the disease, for a rapid rate in patients with bone pain and anemia suggests multiple myeloma."},
